## Verdict

Passed. `studio/briefs/W-110.md` carries all six design-lex sections (Intent,
Files owned, Interfaces, Behaviours to test, Acceptance, Out of scope) plus
Measured present state, Compatibility contract, Migration, Stop conditions,
Stated residuals and Follow-on filings, and is ready for a builder.

## Grounding

Nothing in the spec is recalled. Every claim in *Measured present state* was
probed on this checkout: the served console was built, started against a
throwaway copy of `examples/sample-studio`, and walked in the repo's own
chromium. The probes established, among others, that `aria-current` is absent
from every nav-rail link; that `Officina.tsx` never calls `fetchActa`, so
`/api/acta` is never requested and the fasti strip is permanently hollow; that
`/api/aerarium` answers `[]` for a period with no allowance file, leaving the
System status panel empty; that every served-origin response is 200 while the
page's Google-Fonts request answers 407 behind a proxy; that `apps/web/dist`
is three weeks older than the source it serves because `test:serve` does not
build; that `redact` masks any 32-character run, so a digest cannot survive a
gate log; and that playwright's `--grep` cannot be anchored with `^` because
the matched string is prefixed by the spec file path.

## Scope

Eight behaviours, each individually red-able from the repo root with no
`--cwd`. Two are served-dist playwright tests, six are node TAP tests. One
seam changes: `localPipeline` names the opus and the officina to a gate
command's environment, because a gate command otherwise cannot write per-opus
artifacts; `docs/ADOPTION.md` and `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` record it in the same
cascade. The screenshot requirement reuses the existing `opus.ui.e2e` rule id
rather than adding one, and no record anywhere is `kind: ui`, so no migration
is needed. Two source fixes touch screens: an ARIA attribute and one missing
fetch call. Neither adds, removes or restyles a visible element; anything that
would is a stop condition, because UI/UX is the Patron's.
